/-!
# `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` is compactly generated for an affine scheme

Let `X` be an affine scheme. Then `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` is generated by a single compact object, namely
the structure sheaf in degree zero. This is the base case of [Stacks, Tag 09IS], the theorem of
Bondal–van den Bergh that `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` has a single perfect generator for every quasi-compact
quasi-separated scheme `X`; the source proves it by the induction principle [Stacks, Tag 08DR]
over the quasi-compact opens of `X`, and the affine case is its base case, deduced there from the
comparison [Stacks, Tag 06Z0] between `D(A)` and `D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec A})`.

That is the proof carried out here, and every input of it is now available at the locally small
model:

* over a ring, `A` in degree zero is a compact object of `D(A)`
  (`StacksDraft.Perfect.isCompactObject_regularModule` together with
  `StacksDraft.Perfect.isCompactObject_derived_single`) and a weak generator
  (`StacksDraft.Perfect.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_regularModule`);
* `~ : D(A) ≌ D(QCoh(𝒪_{Spec A}))` is the `~` edge of [Stacks, Tag 06Z0],
  `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.derivedTildeEquiv`, obtained here as
  `AlgebraicGeometry.tildeEquiv.functor.mapDerivedCategory`;
* the comparison functor `D(QCoh(𝒪_X)) ⥤ D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` of [Stacks, Tag 06VT] is an equivalence on
  every affine scheme, which is
  `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.derivedQuasicoherentComparison_isEquivalence_of_isAffine`;
* compactness and generation both transfer along an additive equivalence commuting with the
  shift, by `CategoryTheory.isCompactObject_iff_isCompactObject_obj` and
  `Stacks.Duality.isZero_of_rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_map_of_equivalence`.

An affine scheme is isomorphic to a spectrum rather than equal to one, so the chain is composed
with the equivalence `QCoh(𝒪_{Spec Γ(X, ⊤)}) ≌ QCoh(𝒪_X)` that the isomorphism
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.isoSpec` induces.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Duality.AffineGeneration.qcohEquivOfSchemeIso` — the equivalence
  `QCoh(𝒪_X) ≌ QCoh(𝒪_Y)` attached to an isomorphism of schemes `X ≅ Y`.
* `Stacks.Duality.AffineGeneration.affineComparison` — the composite equivalence
  `D(Γ(X, ⊤)) ⥤ D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` for `X` affine.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Duality.AffineGeneration.isCompactlyGenerated_derivedCategory_moduleCat` — `D(A)` is
  compactly generated, in the sense of [Stacks, Tag 09SQ].
* `Stacks.Duality.AffineGeneration.exists_isCompactObject_isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_of_isAffine`
  — **[Stacks, Tag 09IS] for `X` affine**: `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` has a single compact generator.
* `Stacks.Duality.AffineGeneration.isCompactlyGenerated_derivedQuasiCoherent_of_isAffine` and
  `Stacks.Duality.AffineGeneration.isCompactlyGenerated_quasiCoherentDerivedCategory_of_isAffine`
  — the same statement in the `CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.IsCompactlyGenerated` form, at the
  two spellings of the category of `𝒪_X`-modules.
* `Stacks.Duality.AffineGeneration.isLeftAdjoint_qcqsRestrictedDerivedPushforward_of_isAffine` and
  its exact companion — the conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 0A9E] for a quasi-compact
  quasi-separated morphism out of an affine scheme into a quasi-compact scheme.
* `Stacks.Duality.AffineGeneration.isLeftAdjoint_derivedQuasiCoherentι_of_isAffine` and its exact
  companion — **[Stacks, Tag 0CR0] with no hypothesis** for an affine scheme.

## Implementation notes

**What is proved and what is not.** [Stacks, Tag 09IS] asserts for every quasi-compact
quasi-separated `X` the existence of a *perfect* object `P` of `D(𝒪_X)` with
`E = 0 ↔ Hom(P[n], E) = 0` for all `n`, for `E` in `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)`. Two things separate what is
registered here from that.

*The hypothesis is affineness, not quasi-compactness and quasi-separatedness.* The source runs
the induction principle [Stacks, Tag 08DR] over the quasi-compact opens, which the library has as
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.InductionPrinciple.induction_isCompact_open`, and the abstract
inductive step is available too, as
`Stacks.Duality.OpenImmersion.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_biprod_of_detection` — as are both
implications of [Stacks, Tag 09IR] on an affine scheme and the vanishing of the Koszul object on
the complement of its zero locus,
`Stacks.Koszul.OpenComplement.isZero_derivedRestrict_koszulObject`. What is missing is what the
inductive step must be *fed*:

* [Stacks, Tag 09IQ] at a quasi-compact quasi-separated scheme, which produces the perfect object
  of `D(𝒪_X)` whose restriction to the quasi-compact open has the generator there as a direct
  summand. The library has the affine case only,
  `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.OpenLift.exists_isPerfectComplex_retract_restrict_of_isPerfect`, and at
  `CategoryTheory.HasDerivedCategory.standard`; the source deduces the general case from
  [Stacks, Tag 09IM], itself needing [Stacks, Tag 08EK] and [Stacks, Tag 08EH], none of the three
  being in the library.
* the implication *perfect ⇒ compact* of [Stacks, Tag 09M1], which the induction needs in order
  for the generator it builds to be compact and not merely generating. The source draws it from
  the identification `Hom_{D(𝒪_X)}(K, M) = H⁰(X, K^∨ ⊗^L M)` of [Stacks, Tag 08DQ]. That
  identification is *present*, contrary to what this bullet said and to what the
  `@[stacks 09IS]` clause below still says: it is
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.bijective_derivedTensorDualGlobalSectionsMap_of_isPerfect` and
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedTensorDualGlobalSectionsAddEquiv` of
  `StacksFrontier/Topology/Sheaves/Cohomology/InternalHom/PerfectDualGlobalSections.lean`, and at
  the site level `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedTensorDualGlobalSectionsAddEquiv` of
  `StacksFrontier/Topology/Sheaves/Cohomology/InternalHom/PerfectDualSiteGlobalSections.lean`,
  the latter with its naturality in the second variable
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedTensorDualGlobalSectionsMap_naturality`). What is
  missing is the deduction of 09M1 from the formula, not the formula.
* the three geometric hypotheses that
  `Stacks.Duality.OpenImmersion.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_biprod_of_detection` carries — that
  the Koszul object pushed forward to `X` restricts to zero on the open, that `Rj_*` is fully
  faithful, and the detection statement of [Stacks, Tag 09IR] for that pushforward — at the
  generality of an open immersion into `X` rather than of the inclusion of the complement of a
  zero locus in an affine scheme. Carrying them across is [Stacks, Tag 08DF], the identification
  of `R(V → X)_*` with extension by zero, together with [Stacks, Tag 08DP]; both are registered,
  but not composed with the above.

*These are gaps in the source's route, not in the result.* Compact generation of `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)`
at a quasi-compact quasi-separated `X` is **proved**, by a different route:
`Stacks.Duality.QcqsGeneration.isCompactlyGenerated_quasiCoherentDerivedCategory` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Duality/CompactGeneration/QcqsCompactGeneration.lean`, proved by
induction over a finite affine cover with this file's affine case as the base and so needing
neither [Stacks, Tag 09IQ] at a quasi-compact quasi-separated scheme nor the
*perfect ⇒ compact* implication. So nothing above should be read as saying that the
quasi-compact quasi-separated case of [Stacks, Tag 09IS] is blocked on 09IQ; it is not. What
that route does not deliver — and what the `@[stacks 09IS]` registration is withheld for there
— is the *perfectness* of the generators, which is [Stacks, Tag 09M1].

*The generator is exhibited as compact, not as perfect.* It is the image of `Γ(X, ⊤)` in degree
zero under the comparison chain above, which is the structure sheaf in degree zero, the source's
own generator for an affine scheme; and over an affine scheme perfect and compact coincide, by
[Stacks, Tag 07LT] (`StacksDraft.Perfect.isPerfect_iff_isCompactObject`) carried across
[Stacks, Tag 06Z0]. That carrying is not performed here, because the library's statement of it,
`AlgebraicGeometry.isCompactObject_iff_isPerfect_spec`, is elaborated under
`attribute [local instance] CategoryTheory.HasDerivedCategory.standard` and so is a statement
about a different derived category; see below. Compactness, not perfectness, is what the
consumers of the tag — Brown representability through
`CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.IsCompactlyGenerated` — ask for.

**The model.** Everything here is at the locally small derived category of
`StacksFrontier/Homology/DerivedCategory/LocallySmall.lean`, supplied by instance search:
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.hasDerivedCategory`, `ModuleCat.hasDerivedCategory` and
`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.hasDerivedCategoryQuasicoherent`. This is forced rather than chosen. Brown
representability, [Stacks, Tag 0A8G], asks for direct sums indexed by the *morphism* universe of
the category, and only at this model is that universe `u`; with
`CategoryTheory.HasDerivedCategory.standard` the morphisms live in `Type (u + 1)` and the
hypothesis is false rather than unavailable. The universe `u` in `IsCompactlyGenerated.{u}` and
in `IsCompactObject.{u}` is that morphism universe throughout.

**Crossing between the two models is possible; what does not cross is the universe.** The
remarks above and below that a statement at `HasDerivedCategory.standard` "is a statement about
a different derived category" say why a given declaration is not *reused verbatim*. They should
not be read as saying that nothing can be carried between the models — a general comparison is
available and has been used:

* `StacksDraft.DerivedModel.modelEquiv` of
  `StacksFrontier/Homology/DerivedCategory/ModelComparison.lean` — an equivalence between any two
  chosen derived categories of the same abelian category, with
  `StacksDraft.Perfect.derivedEquivalenceCommShift` and
  `StacksDraft.Perfect.derivedEquivalence_isTriangulated` of
  `StacksFrontier/Homology/Perfect/Characterizing.lean` making it commute with the shift and be
  triangulated;
* for schemes, `StacksDraft.DerivedModel.schemeModulesComparison` of
  `StacksFrontier/Homology/DerivedCategory/ModelComparisonTransport.lean`, whose two sides are the
  same type on the nose — `StacksDraft.DerivedModel.derivedCategory_eq_standard`, by `rfl`;
* two worked cross-model transports to copy:
  `StacksDraft.CompactDevissage.isIso_of_isIso_app_freeYoneda_anyModel` of
  `StacksFrontier/Homology/Devissage/CompactGenerationOfDiagramsAnyModel.lean`, and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.derivedCategoryB_derivedPushforward_of_qcqs` of
  `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Duality/KoszulOrthogonality/AffineComparison.lean`, which
  transports part (2) of [Stacks, Tag 08D5] off the standard model.

The real caveat is narrower, and it is a universe count rather than a model mismatch.
`CategoryTheory.IsCompactObject.{w}` quantifies over index types in `Type w`, so it is monotone
in `w`, and it transports along an additive equivalence only **at a fixed `w`** — the two
categories being allowed different hom universes. Compactness carried to the standard model
therefore arrives at `w = u`, while every consumer there asks for it at that category's own
hom universe, which is `u + 1`: strictly stronger, and not what the transport delivers.
`StacksFrontier/Homology/Perfect/CompactObjectAnyModel.lean` sets out this count in full and
removes the pin where it can.

**What this does not reach: [Stacks, Tag 0AA2].** The twisted inverse image `i^!` of
`Stacks.Duality.isDerivedSheafHomRightAdjoint_of_fts_closedImmersion` is an explicit parameter
whose existence is [Stacks, Tag 0A9E], and discharging it there is not a matter of supplying
compact generation: that file is elaborated under
`attribute [local instance 10000] CategoryTheory.HasDerivedCategory.standard`, so its
`Stacks.Duality.quasiCoherentDerivedCategory` has morphisms in `Type (u + 1)` and the adjoint it
asks for is a functor at that model. The result below is at the locally small model and has a
different type. Nor can Brown representability be run at the standard model to produce the
adjoint it wants: [Stacks, Tag 0A8G] needs coproducts indexed by the morphism universe, which
there is `u + 1`, and those do not exist in `𝒪_X`-modules — the hypothesis is false rather than
unavailable, which is the whole reason the locally small model exists. Closing
[Stacks, Tag 0AA2] therefore needs
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Duality/ClosedImmersionTwistedInverseImage.lean` transported off
`HasDerivedCategory.standard`, as part (2) of [Stacks, Tag 08D5] recently was, *and* then
[Stacks, Tag 09IS] for the source of the closed immersion, which is an arbitrary object of
`FTS S` and not an affine scheme.

`Stacks.Duality.quasiCoherentDerivedCategory X` and
`(Stacks.Duality.derivedQuasiCoherent X).FullSubcategory` are the same type — the first
is spelled over `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules X` and the second over
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules X.ringCatSheaf` — but the two spellings receive their
`HasDerivedCategory` instance from two separately declared instances, so a statement elaborated
in one spelling is not *found* by instance search in the other. Both are therefore stated, each
proved from the other by `exact`; this is the device of `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.modulesRestrictAlong`.

